{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786914597582},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents, using two data sources:\n1. A CSV of US farmers markets by state: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. A census file with population data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nFollowing the instructions in AGENTS.md, I need to:\n1. Orient first - check if there's a semantic model or existing aliases in the catalog\n2. If not, ingest the data sources as aliases\n3. Use xorq_select to compute the metric\n4. Verify the result with xorq_verify\n5. Check lineage with xorq_check_lineage\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog status and what's available.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's already in the catalog, then ingest and compute this metric."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0168nhJuuphfciZokTFfDyeA","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01MXsLVAMU4Uem3mCjTZVeg4","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":383,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8157,"totalTokens":8550,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0019150000000000003,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01019625,"total":0.01212125},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":232},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914597600,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77WtH917mmetQoZiaus","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0168nhJuuphfciZokTFfDyeA","toolName":"xorq_catalog_info","content":[{"type":"text","text":"path:    /private/tmp/trial-pi-25-3j8jsylj/.xorq/catalog\ncommit:  d805e10a020a\nremotes: (none)\nentries: 0\naliases: 0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914601200},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01MXsLVAMU4Uem3mCjTZVeg4","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914601200},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both data sources. According to the instructions, I should:\n1. Create build scripts under `.xorq/scripts/`\n2. Use `xo.deferred_read_csv(url, con, storage_options=...)` to read from URLs\n3. Build with `xorq build` and add to the catalog\n\nI'll need to create two separate build scripts:\n1. One for the farmers markets data\n2. One for the census population data\n\nThen I'll compose a metric that calculates the per capita rate.\n\nLet me start by creating the directory structure and the build scripts.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty. I need to ingest both data sources. Let me create build scripts to load them into the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01WcQbPP7jwo3PzUhqRb7yGB","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":236,"cacheRead":8157,"cacheWrite":529,"totalTokens":8936,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.00118,"cacheRead":0.0008157,"cacheWrite":0.00066125,"total":0.00267095},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":146},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914601201,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77X9JmxZK9jJAT4ZNwo","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01WcQbPP7jwo3PzUhqRb7yGB","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914604110},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll create the build scripts for both data sources. I need to use the xo module with deferred_read_csv to read from the URLs with proper User-Agent headers.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01213bMbAJ5qsr6aGtmSarCJ","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py","content":"import xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\ncon = xo.duckdb.connect(\":memory:\")\nstorage_options = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst\"})\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=storage_options\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":235,"cacheRead":8686,"cacheWrite":259,"totalTokens":9192,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.001175,"cacheRead":0.0008686000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00032375,"total":0.00237935},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":44},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914604111,"responseId":"msg_011Ce77XQa3U29SpfzSQp6D8","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01213bMbAJ5qsr6aGtmSarCJ","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 297 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786914606693},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me create the build script for the census population data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01QJtkV5tuXtWQnEFuWSGjKs","name":"write","arguments":{"path"